<description>
Recolor every candidate object whose run-compressed shape matches the single prototype object, allowing rotation and reflection.
Input structure
A black-background grid contains exactly two foreground colors: one color forms a single prototype object, and the other forms multiple candidate objects.
Rule
Crop each object to its bbox, collapse adjacent identical rows and columns to remove stretch, and recolor every candidate whose collapsed mask is a rotation or reflection of the prototype's collapsed mask.
Key insight
The prototype is a line-drawing symbol; candidate symbols can be stretched in row/column runs, so matching must compare the compressed topology rather than raw size.
</description>
<annotation>
{
  "type": "move_to_match",
  "src": "candidate objects s in the multi-object foreground color",
  "dst": "single prototype object d in the other foreground color",
  "match_cond": "run-compressed s.shape == run-compressed d.shape up to rotation/reflection",
  "transform": "recolor matched s to d.color; leave nonmatching objects unchanged"
}
</annotation>
<generation_spec>
```yaml
spec:
  grid: 15-19 rows x 15-19 cols, square, black background
  colors: exactly 2 non-black foreground colors; prototype_color has 1 connected component, candidate_color has 6-8 [observed]
  prototype:
    single 4-connected component; bbox 2-5 rows x 2-5 cols [observed]
    a line-drawing symbol (open or closed frame/cross); density 0.78-0.89
    compressed shape 2-5 rows x 2-5 cols (may equal raw shape)
  candidates:
    6-8 objects of the other foreground color, each 4-connected
    bbox 2-5 rows x 2-5 cols per object; density 0.55-0.89
    matching candidates (3-4 per grid): compressed shape equals prototype compressed shape under rot90/flip
    distractors (3-5 per grid): compressed shape differs from all 8 prototype orientations
    stretching: matching candidates can duplicate adjacent identical rows/cols (stretch factor 1.0-2.3 per axis)
  layout: all components separated by >=2 Chebyshev distance; no overlap or adjacency
  output: recolor each matching candidate to prototype_color; distractors and prototype unchanged
generation_strategy:
  approach: output-first
  steps:
    1. Pick grid size (15-19, square) and two distinct non-black colors (proto_color, cand_color).
    2. Design a prototype shape as a small boolean mask (compressed 2-4 rows x 2-4 cols) representing a line-drawing symbol with >=1 interior hole or cross structure. Compute all 8 rot/flip signatures.
    3. Generate 3-4 matching candidate masks by picking a rotation/reflection of prototype, then stretching random rows/cols by duplicating 0-2 adjacent identical rows and 0-2 adjacent identical cols.
    4. Generate 3-5 distractor masks as small line-drawings whose compressed signature does NOT appear in the 8 prototype signatures. Verify mismatch. Optionally stretch them too.
    5. Place prototype (in proto_color) and all candidates+distractors (in cand_color) on the grid with >=2 Chebyshev gap between any two objects. Use greedy or random placement with rejection.
    6. Output = copy of input with matching candidates recolored to proto_color.
```
</generation_spec>
