<description>
Copy the unique colored sprite tile into every tiled cell marked by an internal separator-colored pixel.

Input structure
- Full same-color separator rows and columns partition the grid into equal rectangular tiles.
- One tile contains the only non-background, non-separator colored sprite.
- Target tiles are otherwise background-colored but contain at least one internal pixel of the separator color.

Rule
- Keep the separator lines and the source sprite tile unchanged.
- Replace each marked target tile with an exact copy of the source tile.
- Unmarked background-only tiles remain unchanged.

Key insight
- The internal separator-colored pixels are placement markers; the single colored tile is the template to stamp into those marked cells.
</description>
<annotation>
{
  "type": "move_to_match",
  "src": "unique colored sprite tile s in the separator grid",
  "dst": "marked background tile d containing an internal separator-colored marker pixel",
  "match_cond": "every marked d receives the same unique s",
  "transform": "replace d with an exact copy of s, erasing the marker"
}
</annotation>
<generation_spec>
```yaml
spec:
  grid:
    structure: separator rows and columns of a single color divide grid into equal rectangular tiles
    tile_grid: 3-4 rows x 3-4 cols of tiles
    tile_size: 3x3 or 5x5 (always odd, always square) [observed]
    overall_size: tile_rows * tile_size + (tile_rows - 1) separator lines
  colors:
    exactly 3 distinct colors - separator, background, sprite
    separator: forms all full-spanning rows and columns (1px wide)
    background: fills all non-sprite, non-separator pixels; dominant color
  source_tile:
    count: exactly 1 tile contains sprite-colored pixels
    content: single-color sprite on background; no separator pixels inside
    sprite_pixels: 3-11 pixels, 30-45% of tile area [observed]
    connectivity: 1-5 connected components [observed]
  marker_tiles:
    count: 3-5 tiles marked for copying
    marker: exactly 1 separator-colored pixel at the tile center
    rest of tile is pure background
  empty_tiles:
    all remaining tiles are pure background (no sprite, no marker)
  rule: |
    Copy the source tile into every marker tile (replacing marker).
    Source tile, empty tiles, and separator lines stay unchanged.

generation_strategy:
  approach: output-first
  steps:
    1. Pick 3 colors (separator, background, sprite) all distinct.
    2. Choose tile_rows, tile_cols in [3,4]; tile_size in {3, 5} (odd).
    3. Build grid of bg filled tiles separated by single-pixel separator lines.
    4. Design a sprite pattern within one tile (single color on bg, >=2 pixels).
    5. Place sprite in one random tile position (the source tile).
    6. Choose 3-5 other tile positions as marked tiles; place a single
       separator-colored pixel at the center of each (this is the input).
    7. Output is derived by replacing each marked tile with the source tile.
```
